  "quotes": [
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well, then,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "if you don’t know what to uglify is, you _are_ a simpleton."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What else had you to learn?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well, there was Mystery,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "—Mystery, ancient and modern, with Seaography: then Drawling—the Drawling-master was an old conger-eel, that used to come once a week: _he_ taught us Drawling, Stretching, and Fainting in Coils."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What was _that_ like?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well, I can’t show it you myself,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I’m too stiff. And the Gryphon never learnt it."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Hadn’t time,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I went to the Classics master, though. He was an old crab, _he_ was."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I never went to him,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "he taught Laughing and Grief, they used to say."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "So he did, so he did,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "And how many hours a day did you do lessons?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Ten hours the first day,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "nine the next, and so on."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What a curious plan!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That’s the reason they’re called lessons,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "because they lessen from day to day."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Then the eleventh day must have been a holiday?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Of course it was,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "And how did you manage on the twelfth?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That’s enough about lessons,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "tell her something about the games now."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Same as if he had a bone in his throat,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You may not have lived much under the sea—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I haven’t,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "—and perhaps you were never even introduced to a lobster—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I once tasted—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "No, never"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "—so you can have no idea what a delightful thing a Lobster Quadrille is!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "No, indeed,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What sort of a dance is it?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Why,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "you first form into a line along the sea-shore—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Two lines!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Seals, turtles, salmon, and so on; then, when you’ve cleared all the jelly-fish out of the way—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "_That_ generally takes some time,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "—you advance twice—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Each with a lobster as a partner!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Of course,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "advance twice, set to partners—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "—change lobsters, and retire in same order,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Then, you know,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "you throw the—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "The lobsters!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "—as far out to sea as you can—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Swim after them!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Turn a somersault in the sea!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Change lobsters again!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Back to land again, and that’s all the first figure,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It must be a very pretty dance,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Would you like to see a little of it?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Very much indeed,"
    }
  ],
  "relationships": []
}

