      "description": "Where Alice and the Duchess met.",
      "kind": "Place",
      "mentions": ["the kitchen"],
      "name": "the kitchen"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "The game going on rather better now; Alice has a flamingo for it.",
      "kind": "Event",
      "mentions": ["The game's"],
      "name": "the game"
    }
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You can't think how glad I am to see you again, you dear old thing!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "herself",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "When _I'm_ a Duchess"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "herself",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I won't have any pepper in my kitchen _at all_. Soup does very well without—Maybe it's always pepper that makes people hot-tempered"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "herself",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and vinegar that makes them sour—and camomile that makes them bitter—and—and barley-sugar and such things that make children sweet-tempered. I only wish people knew _that_: then they wouldn't be so stingy about it, you know—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You're thinking about something, my dear, and that makes you forget to talk. I can't tell you just now what the moral of that is, but I shall remember it in a bit."
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Perhaps it hasn't one"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Tut, tut, child!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Everything's got a moral, if only you can find it."
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "The game's going on rather better now"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "'Tis so"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and the moral of that is—'Oh, 'tis love, 'tis love, that makes the world go round!'"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Somebody said"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "that it's done by everybody minding their own business!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Ah, well! It means much the same thing"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and the moral of _that_ is—'Take care of the sense, and the sounds will take care of themselves.'"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I dare say you're wondering why I don't put my arm round your waist"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "the reason is, that I'm doubtful about the temper of your flamingo. Shall I try the experiment?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "He might bite"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Very true"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "flamingoes and mustard both bite. And the moral of that is—'Birds of a feather flock together.'"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Only mustard isn't a bird"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Right, as usual"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "what a clear way you have of putting things!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It's a mineral, I _think_"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Of course it is"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "there's a large mustard-mine near here. And the moral of that is—'The more there is of mine, the less there is of yours.'"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Oh, I know!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "it's a vegetable. It doesn't look like one, but it is."
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I quite agree with you"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and the moral of that is—'Be what you would seem to be'—or if you'd like it put more simply—'Never imagine yourself not to be otherwise than what it might appear to others that what you were or might have been was not otherwise than what you had been would have appeared to them to be otherwise.'"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I think I should understand that better"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the Duchess",
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "if I had it written down: but I can't quite follow it as you say it."
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That's nothing to what I could say if I chose"
    }
  ],
