      "words": "we’re all mad here. I’m mad. You’re mad."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "How do you know I’m mad?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You must be,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "or you wouldn’t have come here."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "And how do you know that you’re mad?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "To begin with,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "a dog’s not mad. You grant that?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I suppose so,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well, then,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "you see, a dog growls when it’s angry, and wags its tail when it’s pleased. Now _I_ growl when I’m pleased, and wag my tail when I’m angry. Therefore I’m mad."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
