    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A bird hatching eggs that must be on the look-out for serpents night and day and has not had a wink of sleep for three weeks; it took the highest tree in the wood and settles down again into its nest.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "the Pigeon",
        "Pigeon"
      ],
      "name": "the Pigeon"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A footman whom, judging by his face only, Alice would have called a fish; he came running out of the wood and rapped loudly at the door with his knuckles.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "a footman in livery"
      ],
      "name": "a footman in livery"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A footman with a round face and large eyes like a frog; he opened the door.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "another footman in livery"
      ],
      "name": "another footman in livery"
    }
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "As if it wasn’t trouble enough hatching the eggs,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but I must be on the look-out for serpents night and day! Why, I haven’t had a wink of sleep these three weeks!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I’m very sorry you’ve been annoyed,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "And just as I’d taken the highest tree in the wood,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and just as I was thinking I should be free of them at last, they must needs come wriggling down from the sky! Ugh, Serpent!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "But I’m _not_ a serpent, I tell you!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I’m a—I’m a—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well! _What_ are you?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I can see you’re trying to invent something!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I—I’m a little girl,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "A likely story indeed!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I’ve seen a good many little girls in my time, but never _one_ with such a neck as that! No, no! You’re a serpent; and there’s no use denying it. I suppose you’ll be telling me next that you never tasted an egg!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I _have_ tasted eggs, certainly,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but little girls eat eggs quite as much as serpents do, you know."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I don’t believe it,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but if they do, why then they’re a kind of serpent, that’s all I can say."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You’re looking for eggs, I know _that_ well enough; and what does it matter to me whether you’re a little girl or a serpent?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It matters a good deal to _me_,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but I’m not looking for eggs, as it happens; and if I was, I shouldn’t want _yours_: I don’t like them raw."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Pigeon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well, be off, then!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Come, there’s half my plan done now! How puzzling all these changes are! I’m never sure what I’m going to be, from one minute to another! However, I’ve got back to my right size: the next thing is, to get into that beautiful garden—how _is_ that to be done, I wonder?"
    }
  ],
  "relationships": []
}

