      "words": "—or next day, maybe"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "How am I to get in?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Frog-Footman",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "_Are_ you to get in at all?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Frog-Footman",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That's the first question, you know."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It's really dreadful"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "the way all the creatures argue. It's enough to drive one crazy!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Frog-Footman",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I shall sit here"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Frog-Footman",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "on and off, for days and days."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "But what am _I_ to do?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Frog-Footman",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Anything you like"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Oh, there's no use in talking to him"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "he's perfectly idiotic!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "There's certainly too much pepper in that soup!"
    }
  ],
  "relationships": []
}

{
  "entities": [
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A girl at the tea-party who sighs wearily, thinks asking riddles that have no answers a waste of time, speaks of beating time when learning music, and is asked to tell a story.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["Alice", "the young lady"],
      "name": "Alice"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A hare at the tea-party who says \u2018Nor I\u2019, whispers that it only wishes it were half-past one, and interrupts to change the subject and ask for a story; the Hatter points at it with his tea spoon and says it went mad just before last March.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["the March Hare"],
      "name": "March Hare"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A hatter at the tea-party who says Time is \u2018him\u2019 and won\u2019t stand beating, that he quarrelled with Time last March at the great concert given by the Queen of Hearts, and that it is always six o\u2019clock, so it is always tea-time and the party keeps moving round as the things get used up.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["the Hatter"],
      "name": "Hatter"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A dormouse at the tea-party who sleeps at the table, sings \u2018Twinkle, twinkle\u2019 in its sleep until it is pinched to make it stop, denies being asleep, and tells the story of three little sisters who lived at the bottom of a well on treacle.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["the Dormouse", "Dormouse"],
      "name": "Dormouse"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "The queen who gave the great concert at which the Hatter had to sing; she jumped up, bawled that he was murdering the time and called \u2018Off with his head!\u2019, and ever since Time won\u2019t do a thing the Hatter asks.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["the Queen of Hearts", "the Queen"],
      "name": "Queen of Hearts"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Time personified, whom the Hatter calls \u2018him\u2019; he won\u2019t stand beating, would do almost anything for those who keep on good terms with him, but since quarrelling with the Hatter he won\u2019t do a thing the Hatter asks, and it is always six o\u2019clock.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["Time"],
      "name": "Time"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "One of the three little sisters in the Dormouse\u2019s story, who lived at the bottom of a well and lived on treacle.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["Elsie"],
      "name": "Elsie"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "One of the three little sisters in the Dormouse\u2019s story, who lived at the bottom of a well and lived on treacle.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["Lacie"],
      "name": "Lacie"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "One of the three little sisters in the Dormouse\u2019s story, who lived at the bottom of a well and lived on treacle.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": ["Tillie"],
      "name": "Tillie"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "The three little sisters of the Dormouse\u2019s story, named Elsie, Lacie, and Tillie, who lived at the bottom of a well and lived on treacle.",
      "kind": "Group",
      "mentions": ["three little sisters"],
      "name": "three little sisters"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A concert given by the Queen of Hearts at which the Hatter had to sing \u2018Twinkle, twinkle, little bat!\u2019; the Queen jumped up, bawled that he was murdering the time and called \u2018Off with his head!\u2019, and the Hatter says it was there he quarrelled with Time last March.",
      "kind": "Event",
      "mentions": ["the great concert given by the Queen of Hearts"],
      "name": "the great concert given by the Queen of Hearts"
    }
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "March Hare",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Nor I,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I think you might do something better with the time,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "than waste it in asking riddles that have no answers."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "If you knew Time as well as I do,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "you wouldn\u2019t talk about wasting _it_. It\u2019s _him_."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I don\u2019t know what you mean,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Of course you don\u2019t!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I dare say you never even spoke to Time!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Perhaps not,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but I know I have to beat time when I learn music."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Ah! that accounts for it,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "He won\u2019t stand beating. Now, if you only kept on good terms with him, he\u2019d do almost anything you liked with the clock. For instance, suppose it were nine o\u2019clock in the morning, just time to begin lessons: you\u2019d only have to whisper a hint to Time, and round goes the clock in a twinkling! Half-past one, time for dinner!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "March Hare",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I only wish it was,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That would be grand, certainly,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but then\u2014I shouldn\u2019t be hungry for it, you know."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Not at first, perhaps,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but you could keep it to half-past one as long as you liked."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Is that the way _you_ manage?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Not I!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "We quarrelled last March\u2014just before _he_ went mad, you know\u2014"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "\u2014it was at the great concert given by the Queen of Hearts, and I had to sing"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Twinkle, twinkle, little bat! How I wonder what you\u2019re at!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You know the song, perhaps?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I\u2019ve heard something like it,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It goes on, you know,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "in this way:\u2014"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Up above the world you fly, Like a tea-tray in the sky. Twinkle, twinkle\u2014"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Dormouse",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "_Twinkle, twinkle, twinkle, twinkle_\u2014"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well, I\u2019d hardly finished the first verse,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "when the Queen jumped up and bawled out, \u2018He\u2019s murdering the time! Off with his head!\u2019"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Queen of Hearts",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "He\u2019s murdering the time! Off with his head!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "How dreadfully savage!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "And ever since that,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "he won\u2019t do a thing I ask! It\u2019s always six o\u2019clock now."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Is that the reason so many tea-things are put out here?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Yes, that\u2019s it,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "it\u2019s always tea-time, and we\u2019ve no time to wash the things between whiles."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Then you keep moving round, I suppose?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Exactly so,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "as the things get used up."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "But what happens when you come to the beginning again?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "March Hare",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Suppose we change the subject,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "March Hare",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I\u2019m getting tired of this. I vote the young lady tells us a story."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I\u2019m afraid I don\u2019t know one,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "March Hare",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Then the Dormouse shall!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Then the Dormouse shall!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Dormouse",
      "speaker": "March Hare",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Wake up, Dormouse!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Dormouse",
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Wake up, Dormouse!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Dormouse",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I wasn\u2019t asleep,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Dormouse",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I heard every word you fellows were saying."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "March Hare",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Tell us a story!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Yes, please do!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "And be quick about it,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Hatter",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "or you\u2019ll be asleep again before it\u2019s done."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Dormouse",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Once upon a time there were three little sisters,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Dormouse",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and their names were Elsie, Lacie, and Tillie; and they lived at the bottom of a well\u2014"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What did they live on?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Dormouse",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "They lived on treacle,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "They couldn\u2019t have done that, you know,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "they\u2019d have been ill."
    }
  ],
