{
  "entities": [
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A girl whom the Mock Turtle and the Gryphon dance round and round while the Mock Turtle sings, and who talks with them about the whiting.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "Alice"
      ],
      "name": "Alice"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Dances round Alice with the Gryphon, sings a song about a whiting and a snail, and talks with Alice about whitings.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "the Mock Turtle"
      ],
      "name": "Mock Turtle"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Dances round Alice with the Mock Turtle and explains to Alice why whitings go with the lobsters to the dance and do the boots and shoes under the sea.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "the Gryphon"
      ],
      "name": "Gryphon"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A fish in the Mock Turtle's song who asks a snail to come and join the dance.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "a whiting",
        "the whiting",
        "his scaly friend"
      ],
      "name": "Whiting"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "A snail in the Mock Turtle's song who replies \"Too far, too far!\" and would not join the dance.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "a snail",
        "the snail",
        "beloved snail"
      ],
      "name": "Snail"
    }
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Very much indeed,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Gryphon",
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Come, let's try the first figure!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Gryphon",
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "We can do without lobsters, you know. Which shall sing?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Oh, _you_ sing,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I've forgotten the words."
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Snail",
      "speaker": "Whiting",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Will you walk a little faster?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Whiting",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "There's a porpoise close behind us, and he's treading on my tail. See how eagerly the lobsters and the turtles all advance! They are waiting on the shingle—will you come and join the dance? Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, will you join the dance? Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, won't you join the dance?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Whiting",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You can really have no notion how delightful it will be When they take us up and throw us, with the lobsters, out to sea!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Snail",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Too far, too far!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Whiting",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What matters it how far we go?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Whiting",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "There is another shore, you know, upon the other side. The further off from England the nearer is to France— Then turn not pale, beloved snail, but come and join the dance. Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, will you join the dance? Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, won't you join the dance?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Thank you, it's a very interesting dance to watch,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and I do so like that curious song about the whiting!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Oh, as to the whiting,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "they—you've seen them, of course?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Yes,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I've often seen them at dinn—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I don't know where Dinn may be,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but if you've seen them so often, of course you know what they're like."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I believe so,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "They have their tails in their mouths—and they're all over crumbs."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You're wrong about the crumbs,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "crumbs would all wash off in the sea. But they _have_ their tails in their mouths; and the reason is—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Gryphon",
      "speaker": "Mock Turtle",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Tell her about the reason and all that,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "The reason is,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "that they _would_ go with the lobsters to the dance. So they got thrown out to sea. So they had to fall a long way. So they got their tails fast in their mouths. So they couldn't get them out again. That's all."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Thank you,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "it's very interesting. I never knew so much about a whiting before."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I can tell you more than that, if you like,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Do you know why it's called a whiting?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I never thought about it,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Why?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "_It does the boots and shoes_,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Does the boots and shoes!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Why, what are _your_ shoes done with?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I mean, what makes them so shiny?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "They're done with blacking, I believe."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Boots and shoes under the sea,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "are done with a whiting. Now you know."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "And what are they made of?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Soles and eels, of course,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Gryphon",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "any shrimp could have told you that."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "If I'd been the whiting,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I'd have said to the porpoise, 'Keep back, please: we don't want _you_ with us!'"
    }
  ],
