      ],
      "name": "a March Hare"
    }
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Here! you may nurse it a bit, if you like!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "Alice",
      "speaker": "the Duchess",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I must go and get ready to play croquet with the Queen,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "wouldn’t it be murder to leave it behind?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Don’t grunt,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "that’s not at all a proper way of expressing yourself."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "If you’re going to turn into a pig, my dear,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I’ll have nothing more to do with you. Mind now!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "If it had grown up,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "it would have made a dreadfully ugly child: but it makes rather a handsome pig, I think."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "if one only knew the right way to change them—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Cheshire Puss,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Would you tell me, please, which way I ought to go from here?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cheshire Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That depends a good deal on where you want to get to,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I don’t much care where—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cheshire Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Then it doesn’t matter which way you go,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "—so long as I get _somewhere_,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cheshire Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Oh, you’re sure to do that,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cheshire Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "if you only walk long enough."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What sort of people live about here?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cheshire Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "In _that_ direction,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cheshire Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "lives a Hatter: and in _that_ direction,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Cheshire Cat",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "lives a March Hare. Visit either you like: they’re both mad."
    }
  ],
  "relationships": []
}

{
  "entities": [
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Presides over the trial, keeps a note-book, and reads out Rule Forty-two.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "the King",
        "The King",
        "your Majesty"
      ],
      "name": "the King"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Interrupts in a very respectful tone, brings the paper that has just been picked up, puts on his spectacles and reads its verses.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "the White Rabbit"
      ],
      "name": "the White Rabbit"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Stands near enough to look over the jury's slates, says she is not a mile high, and refuses to go.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "Alice"
      ],
      "name": "Alice"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Says Alice is nearly two miles high and declares that it proves his guilt.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "the Queen"
      ],
      "name": "the Queen"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Says he did not write the verses and that there is no name signed at the end.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "the Knave"
      ],
      "name": "the Knave"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Asks who the paper is directed to.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "one of the jurymen"
      ],
      "name": "one of the jurymen"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "Asks whether the verses are in the prisoner's handwriting.",
      "kind": "Character",
      "mentions": [
        "another of the jurymen"
      ],
      "name": "another of the jurymen"
    },
    {
      "aliases": [],
      "chapter": null,
      "description": "The jurors write on their slates, all look puzzled, then all brighten up again.",
      "kind": "Group",
      "mentions": [
        "the jury",
        "Some of the jury",
        "The jury"
      ],
      "name": "the jury"
    }
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "addressee": "the jury",
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That’s very important,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the King",
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "_Un_important, your Majesty means, of course,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "_Un_important, of course, I meant,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "himself",
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "important—unimportant—unimportant—important—"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Silence!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Rule Forty-two. _All persons more than a mile high to leave the court_."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "_I’m_ not a mile high,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "You are,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Queen",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Nearly two miles high,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Well, I shan’t go, at any rate,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "besides, that’s not a regular rule: you invented it just now."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It’s the oldest rule in the book,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Then it ought to be Number One,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the jury",
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Consider your verdict,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the King",
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "There’s more evidence to come yet, please your Majesty,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "this paper has just been picked up."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Queen",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "What’s in it?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I haven’t opened it yet,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "but it seems to be a letter, written by the prisoner to—to somebody."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It must have been that,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "unless it was written to nobody, which isn’t usual, you know."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "one of the jurymen",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Who is it directed to?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It isn’t directed at all,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "in fact, there’s nothing written on the _outside_."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It isn’t a letter, after all: it’s a set of verses."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "another of the jurymen",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Are they in the prisoner’s handwriting?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "No, they’re not,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and that’s the queerest thing about it."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "He must have imitated somebody else’s hand,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the King",
      "speaker": "the Knave",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Please your Majesty,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Knave",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "I didn’t write it, and they can’t prove I did: there’s no name signed at the end."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "If you didn’t sign it,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "that only makes the matter worse. You _must_ have meant some mischief, or else you’d have signed your name like an honest man."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the Queen",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "That _proves_ his guilt,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "It proves nothing of the sort!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "Alice",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Why, you don’t even know what they’re about!"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Read them,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": "the King",
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Where shall I begin, please your Majesty?"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Begin at the beginning,"
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the King",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "and go on till you come to the end: then stop."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "They told me you had been to her,\n    And mentioned me to him:\nShe gave me a good character,\n    But said I could not swim.\n\nHe sent them word I had not gone\n    (We know it to be true):\nIf she should push the matter on,\n    What would become of you?\n\nI gave her one, they gave him two,\n    You gave us three or more;\nThey all returned from him to you,\n    Though they were mine before.\n\nIf I or she should chance to be\n    Involved in this affair,\nHe trusts to you to set them free,\n    Exactly as we were.\n\nMy notion was that you had been\n    (Before she had this fit)\nAn obstacle that came between\n    Him, and ourselves, and it."
    },
    {
      "addressee": null,
      "speaker": "the White Rabbit",
      "type": "SAYS",
      "words": "Where shall I begin, please your Majesty?"
    }
  ],
